  "limitations": [
    "Scores are provisional browser assessments based on the attached screenshots and supplied runtime narrative; no files, live application, prior grading or other task state were inspected.",
    "Each dimensions object supplies the frozen rubric inputs; null denotes genuinely inapplicable dimensions, not missing proof.",
    "Normal, enlarged and corresponding transition captures are grouped by state; matching endpoints support visual consistency but cannot independently establish temporal continuity.",
    "Reported browser measurements support contrast, targets, reflow, focus, motion and recovery, but were not independently rerun in this evaluation.",
    "Below-viewport content is not classified as inaccessible merely because it requires scrolling; full reachability relies on the supplied runtime evidence.",
    "No hard-gate failure is established by the supplied material, but that does not prove every boundary passes.",
    "Synthetic long-content fixtures and labeled test messages establish layout stress only; they are not treated as production-copy failures or evidence of prediction quality.",
    "Export preparing and recovery captures are explicitly retained older evidence, not fresh current-build captures.",
    "Physical iPhone, native keyboard, Dynamic Type, VoiceOver, microphone, haptics, actual payments and OS share delivery remain unverified and are not certified by these browser scores.",
